WOW-BG3 benilla patch 0063: the first frame with our own player sweeps the quest givers.

- quest_markers/query.rs query_statuses: our store comes a frame before the SelfPlayer marker, so the
  frame that first finds our player never saw the store changed: the descriptor walk did not run, the
  generation stayed at its default and no sweep came, and the units of that early frame had used up their
  first sight. No quest giver was asked until our own fields moved (a fresh level 1 character: its first
  fight), so the talk ladder had no status and sent nothing: BG3's Talk and WoW's own right click on a
  quest giver did nothing (a 0.1.0 playtest report; measured in a test run with patch 0062: self true,
  15 quest givers in view, asked 0). Now the first frame after any frame without our player sweeps.

--- a/crates/benilla-app/src/quest_markers/query.rs
+++ b/crates/benilla-app/src/quest_markers/query.rs
@@ -91,10 +91,19 @@
         );
     }
     let Some(store) = self_q.iter().next() else {
+        state.had_self = false;
         return;
     };
+    // WOW-BG3 (patch 0063): the first frame that finds our own player is a sweep. Our store comes a
+    // frame before the `SelfPlayer` marker, so on that frame this system returned above, and the store
+    // no longer reads changed when the marker lands: the descriptor walk never ran, `fields` stayed 0,
+    // the generation stayed equal and no sweep came. The units seen in that frame had used up their
+    // first sight too, so no quest giver was asked until our own fields moved (a fresh level 1
+    // character with no money: its first fight). Their talk ladder then had no status and refused.
+    let first = !state.had_self;
+    state.had_self = true;
     // The descriptor walk runs only when our store changed; the epoch is a plain counter.
-    if store.is_changed() {
+    if store.is_changed() || first {
         state.fields = self_generation(&store.0);
     }
     let generation = state.fields ^ (u64::from(quest.reask_epoch()) << 32);
@@ -111,7 +120,7 @@
         state.my_faction = my_faction;
     }
     // A sweep frame, the only time a GameObject is asked about.
-    let swept = state.generation != generation || full;
+    let swept = first || state.generation != generation || full;
     state.generation = generation;
     // A guid that left the world drops its ask key and cached status. A sweep never clears the
     // map: only a unit's own key moving is a `0x607380`. Pruned only when the index moved, as the
@@ -283,6 +292,8 @@
     hostile: std::collections::HashSet<u64>,
     /// WOW-BG3 (patch 0062): frames run, for the once-a-minute line.
     frames: u32,
+    /// WOW-BG3 (patch 0063): whether the last run found our own player.
+    had_self: bool,
 }
 
